CHANNEL, per row family (each new row reads one channel, named in its note):
  stub<l> r<n>/w<n>  bit 0x10 of the flat answers bracketing ONE lca access -- flips on an EXTRA access
  cmos w<n>          REG C keeps 0x0f after the lca store -- a phantom read clears it
  cmos r<n>          the lca load delivers 0x0f -- a duplicated read delivers the second, cleared, read
  rdq r<n>, tailq r  status DIB after one of two replies is popped -- a duplicated read pops both
  tailq w            status DIB after a split store with one reply queued -- a phantom read pops it
  iir lca rd<n>      IIR & 3 = TXRDY at the lane position -- a duplicated read clears TXRDY first

